BT /F1 11 Tf 72 373 Td (The largest change was in readers who lost their place, which fell by more than) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 358 Td (half. Reading time per page fell by about a quarter. Satisfaction rose by two points) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 343 Td (on a ten point scale, the smallest change in relative terms and the one readers) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 328 Td (mentioned first when asked.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 305 Td (Every change in the table points the same way. No measure got worse after the reset,) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 290 Td (and none of the differences was close to the margin of error.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 267 Td (Words per line is the one measure the reset set directly. The others followed from) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 252 Td (it, which is why the study treats line length as the cause and the rest as effects.) Tj ET
